      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Guard Hook: Write Operation Enforcement\n├── PreToolUse Hook Entry\n│   ├── IsWriteOperation() check \u003c-- 1a\n│   └── Skip if non-write operation \u003c-- skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:42\n├── Task Store Access\n│   └── OpenTasks() from sessionkit \u003c-- 1b\n├── Active Task Resolution\n│   ├── EnsureActive() call \u003c-- 1c\n│   │   ├── GetActive() query \u003c-- 1d\n│   │   └── Add() new task if none \u003c-- 1e\n│   └── Returns (task, created, error) \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:579\n├── Review Status Enforcement\n│   └── DirtyIfReviewed() call \u003c-- 1f\n│       ├── Check if ready_for_review/completed \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:592\n│       ├── Demote to in_progress \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:597\n│       └── Mark review as stale \u003c-- internal/storage/tasks/store.go:601\n└── Graph Relationship Recording\n    └── createModifiedEdge() \u003c-- 1g\n        ├── UpsertNode(task) \u003c-- skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:218\n        ├── UpsertNode(file) \u003c-- skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:230\n        └── UpsertEdge(task→file, modified) \u003c-- skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:244",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen AI agents or developers make code changes, **two critical problems** emerge: (1) edits might happen without any task tracking, making it impossible to understand what work belongs together, and (2) multiple agents might edit the same file simultaneously, causing conflicts. The **task guard hook** solves both problems by intercepting write operations before they execute.\n\nThe system enforces a **task-centric workflow**: every write operation must be associated with an active task. If no task exists, one is auto-created [1c]. More importantly, if a task has been marked as \"ready for review\" or \"completed,\" any new write automatically **demotes it back to in_progress** [1f], ensuring that review status accurately reflects the current state of the code.\n\n## Details\n\n### Write Operation Detection\n\nThe hook first checks whether the incoming tool is a write operation [1a] using cross-platform detection that recognizes both Claude Code tools (Edit, Write, MultiEdit) and canonical tool names (edit.*, fs.write_*). Non-write operations like Read or Grep are immediately approved and skip enforcement.\n\n### Task Store and Auto-Creation\n\nThe system opens a SQLite-backed task store [1b] from `~/.agentctl/storage/tasks.db`. It then calls `EnsureActive()` [1c], which queries for an existing active task [1d]. If none exists, it creates a new task with `StatusPending` [1e] and sets it as active for the workspace. The task title is derived from the tool name and file path (e.g., \"Edit main.go\").\n\n### Review Demotion Logic\n\nAfter ensuring a task exists, the hook calls `DirtyIfReviewed()` [1f] to check if the task is in `ready_for_review` or `completed` status. If so, it **demotes the status to `in_progress`** and marks any passing review as `stale`. This is the **kernel-owned dirtying policy**: agents don't decide when reviews are invalidated—the system enforces it automatically when new writes occur. This ensures that a \"completed\" task always means \"has passed review since the last code change.\"\n\n### Graph Relationship Tracking\n\nFinally, the hook records a **task→file relationship** in the graph store [1g] by creating nodes for both the task and file, then inserting an edge with `EdgeTypeModified`. This enables PageRank to flow from tasks to the files they touch, helping prioritize which files are most actively worked on.\n\n### Modes\n\nThe hook supports two modes via `AGENTCTL_TASK_GUARD_MODE`:\n- **auto** (default): Auto-creates tasks when none exist\n- **strict**: Blocks write operations if no active task exists, forcing explicit task creation"
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Review Demotion: Status Transition from Reviewed to In-Progress",
      "description": "Task store implementation - demotes tasks from ready_for_review or completed status back to in_progress and marks reviews as stale when new writes occur",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "2a",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 586,
          "lineContent": "t, err := s.Get(ctx, taskID)",
          "title": "Retrieve task by ID",
          "description": "Fetches task record including status and review fields from SQLite tasks table"
        },
        {
          "id": "2b",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 592,
          "lineContent": "if t.Status != StatusReadyForReview \u0026\u0026 t.Status != StatusCompleted {",
          "title": "Check if task is reviewed",
          "description": "Only dirty tasks in ready_for_review or completed status; skip pending/in_progress tasks"
        },
        {
          "id": "2c",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 597,
          "lineContent": "t.Status = StatusInProgress",
          "title": "Demote status to in_progress",
          "description": "Core demotion: transitions task status back to in_progress indicating work resumed"
        },
        {
          "id": "2d",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 600,
          "lineContent": "if t.LastReviewStatus == ReviewStatusOK {",
          "title": "Check review status",
          "description": "Only mark passing reviews as stale; failed/pending reviews remain unchanged"
        },
        {
          "id": "2e",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 601,
          "lineContent": "t.LastReviewStatus = ReviewStatusStale",
          "title": "Mark review as stale",
          "description": "Invalidates previous passing review since code has changed after review"
        },
        {
          "id": "2f",
          "path": "internal/storage/tasks/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 604,
          "lineContent": "updated, err := s.Update(ctx, t)",
          "title": "Persist updated task",
          "description": "Executes UPDATE query to save demoted status and stale review marker to database"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Review Demotion Flow (Trace 2)\n└── DirtyIfReviewed() entry \u003c-- 2a\n    ├── Get task from store\n    ├── Check if reviewed status \u003c-- 2b\n    │   └── (ready_for_review OR completed)\n    ├── Demote to in_progress \u003c-- 2c\n    ├── Check if review was OK \u003c-- 2d\n    │   └── Mark review as stale \u003c-- 2e\n    └── Update task in database \u003c-- 2f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen agents or humans edit code that has already passed review, those edits **invalidate the review**. Without automatic tracking, a task marked as \"completed\" or \"ready for review\" could have new changes that were never reviewed, creating a dangerous gap between review status and actual code state.\n\nThe review demotion mechanism solves this by **automatically demoting tasks back to `in_progress`** whenever new write operations occur on reviewed code [2c]. This ensures that the task lifecycle accurately reflects reality: if code changed after review, it needs to be reviewed again before completion.\n\n## Details\n\nThe `DirtyIfReviewed` function [2a] implements a kernel-owned policy that agents cannot bypass. When a write operation triggers the task guard hook, it checks whether the active task is in `ready_for_review` or `completed` status [2b]. These are the only statuses that indicate review has occurred.\n\nIf the task is in one of these reviewed states, the function performs two critical updates:\n\n1. **Status demotion**: Changes `task.Status` to `StatusInProgress` [2c], signaling that work has resumed and the task is no longer in a reviewable state.\n\n2. **Review invalidation**: If the previous review passed (`LastReviewStatus == ReviewStatusOK` [2d]), it marks the review as `ReviewStatusStale` [2e]. This preserves the historical record that a review occurred, but clearly indicates it no longer applies to the current code.\n\nThe updated task is then persisted to the SQLite database [2f]. This demotion happens **before** the write operation executes, ensuring the task state is always consistent with the code state.\n\nTasks in `pending` or `in_progress` status are not affected—they skip the demotion logic entirely since they were never reviewed [2b]. This prevents unnecessary database writes on normal development workflows."
    },
