      "traceTextDiagram": "Hook Dispatcher: PreToolUse Event Flow\n├── Dispatcher.Dispatch() entrypoint \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:122\n│   ├── Find hooks for event \u003c-- 5a\n│   │   └── config.HooksForEvent(EventPreToolUse) \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:129\n│   ├── Filter hooks by matchers \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:137\n│   │   ├── Check if enabled \u0026 matches \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   ├── Match tool kind (write/read/exec) \u003c-- 5c\n│   │   └── Match tool name/path regex \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:245\n│   ├── Execute each matching hook \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:153\n│   │   ├── Create timeout context (2s default) \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:162\n│   │   ├── runner.Run(hookCtx, hook, input) \u003c-- 5d\n│   │   └── Handle errors \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:181\n│   │       └── Apply fail_open policy \u003c-- 5e\n│   ├── Collect outputs \u0026 check blocks \u003c-- 5f\n│   └── Merge all hook outputs \u003c-- 5g\n│       ├── Blocks take precedence \u003c-- internal/hooks/merge.go:15\n│       ├── Concatenate contexts \u003c-- internal/hooks/merge.go:35\n│       └── Last-wins for tool input mutations \u003c-- internal/hooks/merge.go:41\n└── Return merged Result with decision \u003c-- internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:210",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen AI agents or automated tools execute operations like editing files, the system needs to **intercept and enforce policies** before those operations run. The hook dispatcher solves this by routing **PreToolUse events** to enforcement hooks (like task_guard and file_guard) that can approve, block, or modify operations based on workspace rules. Without this, there's no way to ensure that write operations have an active task, prevent concurrent file edits, or enforce review gates.\n\n## Details\n\n### Event Routing\n\nThe dispatcher receives a **PreToolUse event** with tool metadata (name, input, kind) and looks up registered hooks for that event type [5a]. Each hook can specify **matchers** to filter when it runs—for example, only triggering on write operations or specific file paths [5b].\n\n### Tool Classification\n\nHooks use **tool kind matching** to target categories of operations: `write` (Edit, Write, fs.write_*), `read` (Read, fs.read_*), `exec` (Bash, tests.*), or `search` (Grep, code.search_*) [5c]. This allows hooks like task_guard to run only on write operations without hardcoding every possible tool name.\n\n### Execution Model\n\nFor each matching hook, the dispatcher creates a **timeout context** (default 2 seconds) and executes the hook via SkillRunner or ShellRunner [5d]. Hooks return a decision: **approve**, **block**, or **none** (advisory). If a hook errors, the `fail_open` flag determines whether to treat it as a no-op or block the operation [5e].\n\n### Output Merging\n\nAfter all hooks execute, the dispatcher **merges their outputs** [5g]. The merge logic is conservative: **any block wins** (operation is blocked if any hook blocks) [5f], contexts are concatenated for injection into the AI's prompt, and tool input mutations use last-wins semantics. This ensures that the strictest enforcement always applies.\n\n### Integration Points\n\nThe dispatcher is called from tool runners in the engine layer (`internal/engine/tool_runner.go`) before executing tools, and from agent actor implementations (`internal/actor/agent_actor.go`) that need hook enforcement. The result's `Blocked` field and `BlockedBy` hook ID tell callers whether to proceed with the operation."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Three enforcement mechanisms that intercept write operations via PreToolUse hooks: task guard ensures active tasks exist and demotes reviewed tasks back to in_progress, file guard prevents concurrent edits via exclusive/shared reservations, and the hook dispatcher routes events to enforcement skills. Key flows include task auto-creation [1c], review demotion [2c], conflict detection [3d], and hook execution [5d].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Dispatcher[\"Hook Dispatcher Infrastructure\"]\n        5a[\"5a: Find hooks for event\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Filter by matchers\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Match tool kind\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Execute hook with timeout\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Handle fail-open errors\"]\n        5f[\"5f: Check for blocking decision\"]\n        5g[\"5g: Merge hook outputs\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph TaskGuard[\"Task Guard System\"]\n        1a[\"1a: Write operation detection\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Open task store\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Ensure active task\"]\n        1g[\"1g: Create task→file graph edge\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph TaskStore[\"Task Store \u0026 Demotion\"]\n        1d[\"1d: Check existing active task\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Create new task\"]\n        2a[\"2a: Retrieve task by ID\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Check if task is reviewed\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Demote status to in_progress\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Mark review as stale\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Persist updated task\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph FileGuard[\"File Guard System\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Write operation check\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Extract file path\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Open blackboard store\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Check for conflicts\"]\n        3g[\"3g: Create new reservation\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Blackboard[\"Blackboard \u0026 Conflict Detection\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Clean up expired reservations\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Exclusive mode query\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Shared mode query\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Execute conflict query\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Scan conflict details\"]\n        4f[\"4f: Block operation in strict mode\"]\n    end\n\n    PreToolUse[\"PreToolUse Event\"]\n    \n    PreToolUse --\u003e|triggers| 5a\n    5a --\u003e|finds hooks| 5b\n    5b --\u003e|filters by matchers| 5c\n    5b --\u003e|routes to Task Guard| 1a\n    5b --\u003e|routes to File Guard| 3a\n    \n    1a --\u003e|detects write| 1b\n    1b --\u003e|opens store| 1c\n    1c --\u003e|queries active task| 1d\n    1d --\u003e|not found| 1e\n    1c --\u003e|demotes if reviewed| 2a\n    2a --\u003e|retrieves task| 2b\n    2b --\u003e|is reviewed| 2c\n    2c --\u003e|marks stale| 2e\n    2e --\u003e|persists| 2f\n    1c --\u003e|after ensure| 1g\n    \n    3a --\u003e|detects write| 3b\n    3b --\u003e|extracts path| 3c\n    3c --\u003e|opens store| 3d\n    3d --\u003e|checks conflicts| 3e\n    3e --\u003e|applies rules| 4b\n    3e --\u003e|applies rules| 4c\n    4b --\u003e|exclusive mode| 4d\n    4c --\u003e|shared mode| 4d\n    4d --\u003e|executes query| 4e\n    4e --\u003e|found conflicts| 4f\n    4e --\u003e|no conflicts| 3g\n    \n    1a --\u003e|hook execution| 5d\n    3a --\u003e|hook execution| 5d\n    5d --\u003e|handles errors| 5e\n    5e --\u003e|checks blocking| 5f\n    5f --\u003e|merges outputs| 5g\n\n    style Dispatcher fill:#a5d8ff\n    style TaskGuard fill:#b2f2bb\n    style TaskStore fill:#ffec99\n    style FileGuard fill:#fcc2d7\n    style Blackboard fill:#d0bfff"
